; (specified career)
* On June 27, 1959, the artifacts excavated from the ``First and Second Survey'' conducted from 1954 to 1958 were designated as important cultural properties as ``Artifacts excavated from the Okitsumiya Ritual Site of Munakata Shrine, Chikuzen Province.'' (Cultural Properties Protection Committee Notification No. 45, 1952)* On June 30, 1961, unspecified excavated items were added to the above ``Chikuzen Province Munakata Shrine Okitsunomiya Ritual Ruins Excavated Items.'' (Cultural Properties Protection Committee Notification No. 48 of 1963)
* On June 30, 1961, a collection of excavated items that had not yet been subjected to academic research were separately designated as important cultural properties as ``'''Artifacts excavated from the Chikuzen Munakata Shrine Okitsumiya Ritual Site''. (Cultural Properties Protection Committee Notification No. 45, 1963)
* On June 21, 1962, the Important Cultural Property ``Artifacts excavated from the Okitsu-miya Ritual Ruins of Munakata Shrine, Chikuzen Province'' was designated as a ``National Treasure.'' (Cultural Properties Protection Committee Notification No. 32 of 1963)
* On June 15, 1978, a batch of artifacts excavated from the ``Third Survey'' from 1969 to 1971 was designated as an important cultural property as ``Artifacts excavated from the Okitsumiya Ritual Site of Chikuzen Munakata Shrine.'' (Ministry of Education Notification No. 131 of 1978)
* On June 6, 1979, undesignated cultural properties (gilt-bronze takahiki, gilt-bronze incense burner-like products) were added to the Important Cultural Property ``Artifacts excavated from the Chikuzen Munakata Shrine Okitsu-miya Ritual Site'' (designated in 1961). (Ministry of Education Notification No. 114 of 1978)
* On May 29, 2003, the National Treasure "Articles excavated from the Okitsu-miya Ritual Ruins of Chikuzen Munakata Shrine" and the Important Cultural Property "Articles excavated from the Okitsu-miya Ritual Ruins of Chikuzen Munakata Shrine" (1978 After integrating the designated items) and adding undesignated artifacts to this list, they were designated as a national treasure as ``Artifacts excavated from the Okitsu-miya Ritual Site of Munakata Taisha Shrine, Fukuoka Prefecture.'' (Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology Notification No. 102 of 2003)
* On May 29, 2003, an undesignated cultural property was added to the important cultural property ``Artifacts excavated from the Chikuzen Munakata Shrine Okitsu-miya Ritual Site'' (designated in 1961), and the name was changed to ``Artifacts excavated from the Okitsu-miya Ritual Site of Munakata Taisha Shrine, Fukuoka Prefecture''. (Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology Notification No. 105 of 2003)* On June 9, 2006, the National Treasure "Articles excavated from the Okitsu-miya ritual site of Munakata Taisha Shrine, Fukuoka Prefecture" and the Important Cultural Property "Articles excavated from the Okitsu-miya ritual site of Munakata Taisha Shrine, Fukuoka Prefecture" (designated in 1961) were integrated. After adding undesignated cultural properties to this list, they were designated as national treasures as ``Artifacts excavated from the Okitsu-miya ritual site of Munakata Taisha Shrine, Fukuoka Prefecture; (Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology Notification No. 75 of 2006)
